        <headline>Small Craft Advisory issued September 24 at 12:50PM AKDT until September 25 at 5:00PM AKDT by NWS Juneau AK</headline>
        <description>Southeast Alaska Coastal Waters from Dixon Entrance to
Cape Suckling out 100 NM

Wind forecasts reflect the predominant speed and direction
expected. Seas forecasts represent the average of the highest
one-third of the combined windwave and swell height.

UPDATED

...SMALL CRAFT ADVISORY FRIDAY...

.REST OF TODAY...E wind 10 kt. Seas 7 ft.
.TONIGHT...E wind 20 kt. Seas 6 ft.
.FRI...E wind 30 kt. Seas 11 ft.
.FRI NIGHT...E gale to 35 kt. Seas 15 ft. Showers.
.SAT...E gale to 35 kt. Seas 14 ft.
.SUN...E gale to 35 kt. Seas 13 ft.
.MON...E wind 25 kt. Seas 9 ft.
</description>
